; ---- About requester ------------------------------------------------------
MSG_ABOUT_TITLE (120//)
About Formbrod
;
; The first %s is the version and date, e.g. "0.1 (10.11.2026)". The second
; is MSG_ABOUT_LIBAV or MSG_ABOUT_NO_LIBAV.
MSG_ABOUT_TEXT (121//)
Formbrod %s\n\nA video editor for AmigaOS 4.\n\n%s
;
MSG_ABOUT_LIBAV (122//)
Reads and exports video with ffmpeg's libav* libraries.
;
MSG_ABOUT_NO_LIBAV (123//)
Built without ffmpeg: video can't be read or exported.
;
MSG_ABOUT_OK (124//)
OK
;
; ---- Projects ---------------------------------------------------------------
MSG_MENU_NEW (130//)
New
;
MSG_MENU_OPEN (131//)
Open project...
;
MSG_MENU_SAVE (132//)
Save project
;
MSG_MENU_SAVE_AS (133//)
Save project as...
;
MSG_REQ_OPEN_PROJECT (134//)
Open project
;
MSG_REQ_SAVE_PROJECT (135//)
Save project as
;
; Name of a project that hasn't been saved yet.
MSG_UNTITLED (136//)
Untitled
;
; Window title. The first %s is the project's file name (or MSG_UNTITLED),
; the second is " *" when it has unsaved changes and "" otherwise.
MSG_WINDOW_TITLE_PROJECT (137//)
Formbrod - %s%s
;
MSG_STATUS_NEW_PROJECT (138//)
New project
;
; %s is the file path.
MSG_STATUS_SAVED (139//)
Saved %s
;
; %s is the file path.
MSG_STATUS_CANT_SAVE (140//)
Can't save %s
;
; %s is the file path.
MSG_STATUS_OPENED (141//)
Opened %s
;
; %s is the file path, %d how many of its video files weren't found. The
; project file is text, so the paths can be fixed in any text editor.
MSG_STATUS_OPENED_MISSING (142//)
Opened %s. Files not found: %d (fix their paths in the project file)
;
; %s is the file path.
MSG_STATUS_CANT_OPEN_PROJECT (143//)
Can't read %s
;
; The first %s is the file path, %d the line, the second %s one of the
; MSG_PROJECT_ reasons below.
MSG_STATUS_BAD_PROJECT (144//)
%s, line %d: %s
;
MSG_PROJECT_NOT_PROJECT (145//)
not a Formbrod project
;
MSG_PROJECT_TOO_NEW (146//)
made by a newer Formbrod
;
MSG_PROJECT_BAD_LINE (147//)
this line can't be read
;
MSG_PROJECT_BAD_SOURCE (148//)
the clip's source isn't listed
;
MSG_PROJECT_TOO_MANY (149//)
too many files, clips or effects
;
; Saving the project failed because it has never been saved and no file
; was given (ARexx SAVEPROJECT without FILE).
MSG_STATUS_NO_PROJECT_FILE (150//)
The project has no file name yet
;
; The project couldn't be opened. The first %s is the file path, the
; second MSG_PROJECT_NOT_PROJECT or MSG_PROJECT_TOO_NEW.
MSG_STATUS_NOT_OPENED (151//)
%s: %s
;
; Set in at a playhead outside the selected clip (Set out: before its start).
MSG_STATUS_OUTSIDE_CLIP (152//)
Put the playhead inside the clip first
;
; After trimming: file name, then in and out times in the file.
MSG_STATUS_TRIMMED (153//)
%s now runs from %s to %s
;
; After Set out on a still picture: file name, then its new length.
MSG_STATUS_STILL_LENGTH (154//)
%s is now %s long
;
; A typed time that couldn't be read; %s is what was typed.
MSG_STATUS_BAD_TIME (155//)
%s isn't a time; write it like 1:05.5
;
; Trimming that would make the clip end before it starts or go past its file.
MSG_STATUS_BAD_TRIM (156//)
The clip has to end after it starts, and within its file
;
; ---- Unsaved changes requester ---------------------------------------------
MSG_UNSAVED_TITLE (160//)
Unsaved changes
;
; %s is the project's file name.
MSG_UNSAVED_TEXT (161//)
%s has changes that aren't saved.
;
; The buttons, separated by '|'. The last one cancels.
MSG_UNSAVED_BUTTONS (162//)
Save|Discard|Cancel
; ---- Track editor ----
; The name column in front of the film strip, which shows the result.
MSG_TRACK_RESULT (170//)
Result
;
; Track names in the editor, numbered from the bottom one of each kind.
MSG_TRACK_PICTURE (171//)
Video %ld
;
MSG_TRACK_SOUND (172//)
Audio %ld
;
; Shown in the empty space below the tracks.
MSG_TRACK_DROP (173//)
Drop files here: each one gets a track of its own
;
; The clip fields: where the clip starts in the edit, where in its file it
; begins, and how long it is.
MSG_LABEL_FROM_FILE (174//)
From file
;
MSG_HINT_FROM_FILE (175//)
Where in its file the clip begins. Type a time and press Return
;
MSG_HINT_STARTS (176//)
Where the clip starts in the edit. Type a time and press Return: the clips after it move along
;
MSG_HINT_LANES (177//)
Click a clip to select it, drag its ends to trim it. Click a track's name to select the track
;
MSG_MENU_TRACK (178//)
Track
;
MSG_MENU_APPEND_FILE (179//)
Append file...
;
MSG_MENU_MUTE (180//)
Mute audio
;
MSG_MENU_HIDE (181//)
Hide video
;
MSG_MENU_REMOVE_TRACK (182//)
Remove track
;
MSG_STATUS_SELECT_TRACK (183//)
Click a track's name first
;
; %s is the track's name.
MSG_REQ_REMOVE_TRACK (184//)
Remove %s and the clips on it?
;
MSG_REQ_REMOVE_TRACK_BUTTONS (185//)
Remove|Cancel
;
MSG_INSPECTOR_NONE (186//)
No clip selected
;
; Typing Starts earlier than the clip in front of it ends; %s is that time.
MSG_STATUS_TOO_EARLY (187//)
It can't start before %s, where the clip in front of it ends
;
; After typing Starts: the file name and the new start.
MSG_STATUS_MOVED (188//)
%s now starts at %s
;
